  "title": "Is This the October of Small Ball? It’s Complicated.",
  "subtitle": null,
  "byline": null,
  "publishedAt": null,
  "contentHtml": "<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!NcoY!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b68a482-f230-434b-b027-1c5d614f6cf6_1900x1235.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n<img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!NcoY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5b68a482-f230-434b-b027-1c5d614f6cf6_1900x1235.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"946\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n\n</a><figcaption><strong>Photo credits: </strong>Getty.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Major_League_Baseball_postseason\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2026 MLB postseason</a> has been defined by a lot of things, from the <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/why-should-dodgers-brewers-part-ii\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Brewers-Dodgers NLCS rematch</a> — which <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-dodgers-havent-ruined-baseball\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">feels like a spiritual battle</a> for the Soul of Baseball — to <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/yoshinobu-yamamoto-is-speedrunning\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">epic pitching performances</a>, the <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/guardians-white-sox-is-octobers-battle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cleveland Guardians’ youth</a>, everybody’s <a href=\"https://substack.com/@neilpaine/note/c-356711073\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">weird bullpen-management</a>, the <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/i/218252004/will-the-bye-teams-keep-winning\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ongoing revenge of the first-round bye teams</a>, and the specter of the upcoming lockout <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/mlb/story/_/id/50166698/mlb-playoffs-2026-nlcs-alcs-dodgers-brewers-rays-guardians-payroll-cba-labor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">hanging over all the proceedings</a>. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/subscribe?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p>\n<p>But one of the biggest themes <a href=\"https://abc6onyourside.com/sports/content/guards-ball-vs-small-ball-in-tampa-bay-florida-cleveland-guardians-rays-american-league-championship-series-mlb-baseball-postseason-october-alcs-starts-monday-night\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">has been the sudden resurgence of “small ball” tactics</a> among most of the remaining League Championship Series teams. The Tampa Bay Rays, for instance, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UXgsa7Gydoo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">are known for bunting a LOT</a> — ironic, given they <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/why-baseball-revived-a-60-year-old?utm_source=publication-search\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">have been one of the sport’s foremost analytics laboratories</a> ever <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-phillies-won-the-2008-world-series\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">since the late 2000s</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/fancy-stats/wp/2018/07/10/analytics-killed-the-bunt-now-a-new-data-driven-strategy-could-bring-it-back-to-life/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">bunting was traditionally considered pointless</a> by the nerd-cognoscenti…</p>\n<p>…while Cleveland <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/ClevelandGuardians/comments/1ui5qas/how_do_you_define_guards_ball/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">has its own variant</a> — “Guards Ball” — and the Brewers <a href=\"https://www.mlb.com/news/2026-brewers-offense-what-is-working\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">are notorious for not relying on the home run very much</a>, despite ranking second in park-adjusted runs per game this season. Even the Dodgers, nobody’s idea of a scrappy underdog, were among the MLB leaders at <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/leagues/majors/2026-advanced-batting.shtml#teams_advanced_batting::6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">putting the ball in play</a> and <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/leagues/majors/2026-baserunning-batting.shtml#teams_baserunning_batting::23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">taking the extra-base</a> on the basepaths, even if they <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/leagues/majors/2026-situational-batting.shtml#teams_situational_batting::20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">seldom tried to bunt</a>.</p>\n<p>So there is a distinct sense <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8lmnmtfCO_0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">that old-school baseball has made a grand comeback</a> in these playoffs — and that’s not entirely wrong. But because the postseason can never be that simple, it’s also more complicated than just declaring small-ball “back” or assuming teams have rediscovered some lost secret to winning in October.</p>\n<p>\n          <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/is-this-the-october-of-small-ball\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
